i2c: mv64xxx: enable the reset delay errata on Allwinner A31

The sun6i-a31-i2c compatible sets irq_clear_inverted because its
INT_FLAG bit is write-1-to-clear, but mv64xxx_of_config() never sets
errata_delay for it.  With runtime PM support mv64xxx_i2c_hw_init()
resets the bus before every transfer, and the missing 5 us delay after
that reset leaves the controller stuck: every subsequent xfer reports
"I2C bus locked, block: 1, time_left: 0".  Apply the same errata delay
that is already enabled for the Marvell mv78230 variants.

--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-mv64xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-mv64xxx.c
@@ -920,8 +920,10 @@
 			drv_data->errata_delay = true;
 	}
 
-	if (of_device_is_compatible(np, "allwinner,sun6i-a31-i2c"))
-		drv_data->irq_clear_inverted = true;
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(np, "allwinner,sun6i-a31-i2c")) {
+		drv_data->irq_clear_inverted = true;
+		drv_data->errata_delay = true;
+	}
 
 out:
 	return rc;
